 # log_parser
+
+A small, local Python utility for parsing plain-text log lines. It does not
+call external logging APIs.
+
+## Supported format
+
+```
+<timestamp> <SEVERITY> <message>
+```
+
+For example, `2024-01-01T00:00:00Z INFO boot` becomes:
+
+```python
+{
+    "timestamp": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",
+    "severity": "INFO",
+    "message": "boot",
+}
+```
+
+## Run
+
+Requires Python 3.9+.
+
+```bash
+python -m pytest
+```
+
+## Specification status
+
+The supplied ProjectState has no active requirement IDs, objective, API,
+database, or framework. Consequently, no API or database has been added. The
+existing repository tests provide the concrete parser behavior implemented
+here.
+
+Acceptance evidence: `python -m pytest` passes, and importing
+`app.parser.parse_log` provides the runnable application component.
